WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.783
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 5, Network troubleshooting, which is 24 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.783 --> 00:00:10.318
This lesson covers objective 5 point 2.

00:00:10.318 --> 00:00:15.257
Given a scenario, troubleshoot common cabling and physical interface issues.

00:00:15.257 --> 00:00:21.170
Today's symptom: a link that stays down because transmit and receive are on the wrong pins.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.480
Two older switches, no Auto M D I X, connected with a straight-through cable.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.260
Switch ports are M D I X.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.999
They transmit on pins three and six, and receive on one and two.

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:38.030
A straight-through cable keeps the pins in the same order end to end.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:42.592
So both sides transmit on the same pair, and neither one listens.

00:00:42.592 --> 00:00:44.150
Transmit meets transmit.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:44.670
No link.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.050
Auto M D I X, or a crossover cable, swaps the pairs, so transmit finally meets receive.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:01:02.839
For the exam, two older switches joined by a straight-through cable, with no Auto M D I X, give you no link, because transmit meets transmit.

00:01:02.839 --> 00:01:05.718
A crossover cable or Auto M D I X fixes it.

00:01:05.718 --> 00:01:07.860
That's objective five point two.
